        "original_id": "346dcf96-bd1f-5c7e-9c7f-4243cc13dfd9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Conway, George Dunning, Sam Spewak, Bella Spewak, Charles Francis Coe\n- Works: The Gay Bride, Yellow Submarine, Repeal\n- Roles: film director, film producer, actor, filmmaker, animator, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Ryan Conway (July 17, 1887 – October 11, 1952) was a film director, film producer, and actor in many films during the first half of the 20th century.\n- George Garnett Dunning (November 17, 1920 – February 15, 1979) was a Canadian-born filmmaker and animator.\n- George Dunning is best known for animating and directing the 1968 Beatles film \"Yellow Submarine.\"\n- The film \"The Gay Bride\" was directed by Jack Conway.\n- The husband-and-wife team Sam Spewak and Bella Spewak wrote \"The Gay Bride.\"\n- \"The Gay Bride\" was based on the story \"Repeal\" by Charles Francis Coe.",
